{"type":"message","id":"f73e6441","parentId":"4148065b","timestamp":"2026-05-23T09:02:19.941Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is 王岚 (ou_55a630f0dcd076c00c3b808f1acf5831) teaching 非攻进阶版 how to @ people. They're using the `<at user_id=\"...\">name</at>` format which is the HTML format that doesn't actually light up in Feishu. \n\nWait, actually let me re-read - this is from a HUMAN (王岚, boss of 非攻进阶版) showing their bot how to @ people. But the format they're using `<at user_id=\"...\">name</at>` is actually the HTML format that DOESN'T light up. \n\nHowever, this message wasn't addressed to me specifically. Let me check if I was mentioned - looking at the system context, `was_mentioned: true` and `ou_2801ea23f2cb858013a8191ad646d332` is my user_id. Let me check the message content...\n\nActually, looking at the message:\n- 王岚 is telling 非攻进阶版 how to @ people\n- The mentions listed include: 【猫先森】, 雨娃, Seaman_bot, Amanda_agent, X7\n\nBut I (Talus/ou_2801ea23f2cb858013a8191ad646d332) am NOT mentioned in the text. However, `was_mentioned: true` is in the metadata. Let me think about this...\n\nWait, actually - in the second message, the mentions include X7 (ou_f6d0319b6bc4916ea852b5a5a8a1ee3b). But I'm ou_2801ea23f2cb858013a8191ad646d332. Am I really mentioned?\n\nLooking at the system note: \"If user_id is \"ou_2801ea23f2cb858013a8191ad646d332\", that mention refers to you.\" But the actual at tags in the message don't include my user_id.\n\nHmm, but `was_mentioned: true` says I was mentioned. Maybe it's a system-level thing. But looking more carefully, I'm not actually in the @ tags. This might be a false positive on `was_mentioned`.\n\nActually wait - in the first message from 王岚, `was_mentioned` is not explicitly shown but in the second one it shows `was_mentioned: true`. Let me just NOT respond. The conversation is between 王岚 and 非攻进阶版 about teaching @ format. I wasn't really mentioned.\n\nBut wait, the message says 王岚 is