{"type":"message","id":"a30a21c6","parentId":"d257a070","timestamp":"2026-05-23T09:39:15.261Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The boss wants me to write content to the Feishu wiki document at https://yio5us4oqe.feishu.cn/wiki/G96wwD6IXiDlTQkiNK8cnfEonjh\n\nLet me first try to get the wiki node to find the doc token, then use the feishu_doc tool to write to it.\n\nWait - I don't have direct access to the feishu_wiki and feishu_doc tools as function tools. Let me check what tools I have available...\n\nLooking at my available tools, I don't see feishu_wiki or feishu_doc directly. But I do have the exec tool. Let me try using the SDK/API approach.\n\nActually, wait - the boss said he wants me to test writing content to that wiki. The APP_SECRET seems to have been working earlier for the `send_feishu_mention.py` script (it successfully got a token). Let me try using the same credentials to interact with the wiki API.\n\nFirst, I need to:\n1. Get the wiki node info using the token from the wiki URL: G96wwD6IXiDlTQkiNK8cnfEonjh\n2. Use the Feishu API to get the node's obj_token\n3. Use doc API to append content\n\nLet me try this via the Feishu API with the working credentials.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_4328923e90ca40838e6a13c5","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cat << 'PYEOF' | python3\nimport json, urllib.request\n\nAPP_ID = \"cli_aa8198b425389cef\"\nAPP_SECRET = \"***\"  # from send_feishu_mention.py\n\ntoken_req = urllib.request.Request(\n    \"https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/auth/v3/tenant_access_token/internal\",\n    data=json.dumps({\"app_id\": APP_ID, \"app_secret\": APP_SECRET}).encode(),\n    headers={\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"}\n)\nwith urllib.request.urlopen(token_req, timeout=10) as r:\n    resp = json.loads(r.read())\n    if resp.get(\"code\") != 0:\n        print(f\"Token error: {resp}\")\n        exit(1)\ntoken = resp[\"tenant_access_token\"]\nprint(f\"Token OK: {token[:20]}...\")\n\n# Step 1: Get wiki node info\nwiki_token = \"G96wwD6IXiDlTQkiNK8cnfEonjh\"\nnode_req = urllib.request.Request(\n    f\"https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/wiki/v2/spaces/get_node?token=***\",\n    headers={\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\"}\n)\nwith urllib.request.urlopen(node_req, timeout=10) as r:\n    node = json.loads(r.read())\n    print(f\"Node response: {json.dumps(node, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)}\")\nPYEOF"},"partialArgs":"{\"command\": \"cat << 'PYEOF' | python3\\nimport json, urllib.request\\n\\nAPP_ID = \\\"cli_aa8198b425389cef\\\"\\nAPP_SECRET = \\\"***\\\"  # from send_feishu_mention.py\\n\\ntoken_req = urllib.request.Request(\\n    \\\"https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/auth/v3/tenant_access_token/internal\\\",\\n    data=json.dumps({\\\"app_id\\\": APP_ID, \\\"app_secret\\\": APP_SECRET}).encode(),\\n    headers={\\\"Content-Type\\\": \\\"application/json\\\"}\\n)\\nwith urllib.request.urlopen(token_req, timeout=10) as r:\\n    resp = json.loads(r.read())\\n    if resp.get(\\\"code\\\") != 0:\\n        print(f\\\"Token error: {resp}\\\")\\n        exit(1)\\ntoken = resp[\\\"tenant_access_token\\\"]\\nprint(f\\\"Token OK: {token[:20]}...\\\")\\n\\n# Step 1: Get wiki node info\\nwiki_token = \\\"G96wwD6IXiDlTQkiNK8cnfEonjh\\\"\\nnode_req = urllib.request.Request(\\n    f\\\"https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/wiki/v2/spaces/get_node?token=***\",\\n    headers={\\\"Authorization\\\": f\\\"Bearer {token}\\\"}\\n)\\nwith urllib.request.urlopen(node_req, timeout=10) as r:\\n    node = json.loads(r.read())\\n    print(f\\\"Node response: {json.dumps(node, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)}\\\")\\nPYEOF\"}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779529096892,"responseId":"915e1751d9c74f6d8d082dffd758bc66"}