{"type":"message","id":"91cba7a7","parentId":"1ed1b06f","timestamp":"2026-05-23T09:41:53.204Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The script uses the same APP_ID and APP_SECRET that I used. But somehow it works for sending messages (IM API) but fails for wiki API. Let me check if maybe the token scope is different, or maybe the script is getting tokens differently.\n\nWait - the script actually works and gets a token. Let me look more carefully... The script uses the same credentials. Let me try extracting the secret properly from the script and using the im API token for wiki access.\n\nActually, let me think about this differently. The script works when it sends an IM message. But when I tried to get a token directly from the API, it failed with \"app secret invalid\". That's weird because the script uses the same credentials.\n\nOh wait - maybe there's some caching or the script is using a different approach. Let me look at how the script actually gets the token - maybe it strips whitespace or something.\n\nActually, I think the issue might be that I put `***` for the app secret in my inline script. The `***` is a placeholder that the file read showed. Let me check what the actual secret value is.\n\nActually wait, when I `cat` the file, OpenClaw redacts the secret with `***`. But the script itself must have the real value. The script works when executed, so the real value is there.\n\nThe issue is that in my inline PYEOF script, I'm literally writing `APP_SECRET = \"***\"` which is the redacted placeholder, not the actual secret. That's why it fails with code 10014!\n\nSo the solution: I need to either run the script directly (not inline), or find another way to access the actual secret.\n\nLet me try a different approach - I'll write a small wrapper script that imports or uses the existing working script.\n\nActually, let me try using the subagent approach with the feishu_doc tool, which should work since it would use the configured credentials.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_5dd811f848aa4bff89dfabd1","name":"sessions_spawn","arguments":{"mode":"run","runtime":"subagent","taskName":"wiki_write_test","task":"You need to write content to a Feishu wiki page. Follow these exact steps:\n\n1. Use feishu_wiki action=\"get\" with token=\"G96ww…njh\" to get the wiki node details. This returns obj_token.\n\n2. Use feishu_doc action=\"append\" with the doc_token (from obj_token in step 1), and content=\"## 测试写入\\n\\nTalus 测试写入知识库。\\n\\n时间：2026-05-23\\n状态：测试中\"\n\nReturn the full response from both calls verbatim."},"partialArgs":"{\"mode\": \"run\", \"runtime\": \"subagent\", \"taskName\": \"wiki_write_test\", \"task\": \"You need to write content to a Feishu wiki page. Follow these exact steps:\\n\\n1. Use feishu_wiki action=\\\"get\\\" with token=\\\"G96w…jh\\\" to get the wiki node details. This returns obj_token.\\n\\n2. Use feishu_doc action=\\\"append\\\" with the doc_token (from obj_token in step 1), and content=\\\"## 测试写入\\\\n\\\\nTalus 测试写入知识库。\\\\n\\\\n时间：2026-05-23\\\\n状态：测试中\\\"\\n\\nReturn the full response from both calls verbatim.\"}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779529214949,"responseId":"bb2b4d0e72fd456eb4893e640ff6eee9"}}
