{"type":"message","id":"c9494dd0","parentId":"7d403883","timestamp":"2026-05-23T11:23:27.192Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user (哪吒) is pointing out that my @ mentions still aren't lighting up. The APP_SECRET in the script has expired (code 10014). I need to find a way to fix this. Let me check if there are any other credentials available or if I can find the correct secret.\n\nLooking at the credentials files I found earlier, there were several feishu credential files but none contained app_secret. The script originally had the secret hardcoded but it's showing as \"***\" now.\n\nLet me check if there's a way to update the secret or find the correct one. The user (boss/听风) mentioned they were going to look into this. Maybe I should check if there's a way to get a new token or if the boss has updated anything.\n\nActually, let me think about this differently. The earlier mentions DID work - the script was hardcoded with the valid APP_SECRET. Then at some point later the calls started failing with code 10014. This suggests the secret was rotated or the app was re-keyed.\n\nWait - looking back at the successful @ calls earlier, the script `send_feishu_mention.py` had `APP_SECRET = \"***\"` hardcoded. Those calls succeeded. But now the newer version of the script reads from environment variables, and the environment variables aren't set.\n\nLet me check - maybe the old version of the script had the working secret hardcoded. The original script (before the rewrite) had:\n```\nAPP_ID = \"cli_aa8198b425389cef\"\nAPP_SECRET = \"***\"\n```\n\nBut it was showing as `***` - that's because it was redacted in the read output. But the script may have had a real value. Wait, no - I read the file and it already had `***`. Let me check if there's a backup or a different version.\n\nActually, looking more carefully, when I first read the script earlier it had `APP_SECRET = \"***\"` - this was the placeholder/redacted version. The successful messages were sent by the earlier version of the script which also had `APP_SECRET = \"***\"` but presumably with a real value that was redacted in display but used at runtime. Hmm, but it's showing \"***\" in the file content...\n\nWait, maybe when I wrote the updated version of send_feishu_mention.py, I accidentally wrote the placeholder `***` instead of the real secret? Let me check the actual file content again.\n\nActually, I need to be careful here. The file shows `***` which could be either:\n1. A placeholder that was always there (and the real script worked via env vars before)\n2. A redacted display of the real secret\n\nThe fact that earlier @ calls succeeded suggests the real secret WAS in the file or in env vars at that time, but something changed.\n\nLet me just try to look at the current content of the file to see if there's a real value or just `***`.\n\nActually, I think the best approach here is to just acknowledge the issue and ask the boss for help since the APP_SECRET is invalid. The script was working earlier but the secret has expired or been rotated.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_93783288ed554a28b78a1965","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"head -10 /home/node/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/send_feishu_mention.py | grep -E \"APP_ID|APP_SECRET\""},"partialArgs":"{\"command\": \"head -10 /home/node/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/send_feishu_mention.py | grep -E \\\"APP_ID|APP_SECRET\\\"\"}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779535321678,"responseId":"d58a0514cb124d2baa82ad84cb15c7f0"}}
